  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"4.0.3\"\n\npackage:\n  name: stepup\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/s/stepup/stepup-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: bf96561badb8bb22dfb0971021b3aced4f19ffdd4249b8778a974f8c75f8b733\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - stepup = stepup.core.__main__:main\n      - sb = stepup.core.__main__:sb_main\n      - sc-render-jinja = stepup.core.render_jinja:main\n\n# Notes on the dependencies:\n# stepup.core.watcher imports asyncinotify if sys.platform == \"linux\".\n# It is not made optional because it adds major value.\n# StepUp's macos version is provisional as it cannot use asyncinotify.\n# Similar support for Windows is planned but not yet implemented.\n# (watchdog and watchfiles were considered as alternatives for asyncinotify,\n# but they lack required features.)\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - setuptools >=77.0\n    - setuptools-scm >=8.1\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - __unix\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - __linux\n        - asyncinotify >=4.0.9\n    - if: osx\n      then:\n        - __osx\n    - attrs >=23.1.0\n    - cattrs >=23.2.3\n    - jinja2 >=3.1.6\n    - parse >=1.19.1\n    - path >=16.14.0\n    - pyyaml >=6.0\n    - rich >=13.0.0\n\n# The `if: unix` guards make the build pass on Windows in the staged-recipes CI.\n# They will be removed once the stepup feedstock has been created.\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - stepup.core\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  - script:\n      - stepup --help\n      - sb --help\n      - sc-render-jinja --help\n\nabout:\n  summary: A dynamic Python build tool for reproducible workflows\n  description: |\n    StepUp is a dynamic build tool and a modern alternative to Make.\n    Its defining feature is that workflow generation and execution are unified:\n    a plan.py script defines the initial build steps.\n    While the workflow is being executed, any step can add more steps and\n    dependencies, based on the outputs built so far.\n    This makes StepUp ideal for builds where the full set of dependencies\n    cannot be determined in advance.\n\n    StepUp Core provides the basic framework for StepUp,\n    without any domain-specific features.\n  license: LGPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - LICENSES/LicenseRef-StepUp-Logo-v1.txt\n  homepage: https://reproducible-reporting.github.io/stepup-core/\n  repository: https://github.com/reproducible-reporting/stepup-core/\n  documentation: https://reproducible-reporting.github.io/stepup-core/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - tovrstra\n",
